[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=ROG Claymore
Comment=Apply the saved design at login and wait in the panel
Exec=claymore-gui
Icon=rog-claymore
Terminal=false
StartupNotify=false

# Nothing here says "hide the window", and that is deliberate: 'Start in the
# panel' is a saved preference, so this entry stays a one-liner that cannot
# drift out of sync with what the program actually does.
#
# Turn it on first:
#
#     claymore settings start-in-tray on
#
# or tick 'Start in the panel' in the header. Then copy this file:
#
#     install -Dm644 contrib/autostart/org.claymore.linux.desktop \
#         ~/.config/autostart/org.claymore.linux.desktop
#
# The design applied at login is the one marked 'Load at startup' in the GUI,
# or whichever 'claymore default <name>' names.
#
# 'make install' deliberately does not install this. Starting a program at
# everybody's login is the user's decision, not the package's; the systemd unit
# in contrib/claymore-design.service is the option for people who want the
# design applied with no window at all and nothing left running.
